      "sources_html": "<h2>Sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/regulatory-framework-ai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">European Commission — Regulatory framework for AI</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.nist.gov/itl/ai-risk-management-framework\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NIST — AI Risk Management Framework</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ai-regulation-a-pro-innovation-approach\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UK government — AI regulation: a pro-innovation approach</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cset.georgetown.edu/article/unpacking-the-white-house-national-policy-framework-for-ai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CSET — Unpacking the White House National Policy Framework for AI</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cset.georgetown.edu/publication/china-government-ai-model-use-guidelines\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CSET — China government AI model-use guidelines</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://fpf.org/blog/defining-agentic-why-we-need-a-shared-taxonomy-for-ai-agents/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FPF — Defining “Agentic”</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2025-ai-index-report\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stanford HAI — 2025 AI Index Report</a></li>\n<li>Sibling teaching: <a href=\"../cset-georgetown/index.md\">CSET Georgetown</a> · <a href=\"../fpf/index.md\">FPF</a> · <a href=\"eu-ai-act-risk-based-rules.md\">EU</a> · <a href=\"us-frameworks-nist-and-federal-preemption.md\">US</a> · <a href=\"uk-pro-innovation-and-regulator-coordination.md\">UK</a> · <a href=\"china-governance-and-government-model-use.md\">China</a></li>\n</ul>",
